  "method": "79 of the 1188 muon detectors (MDs): the layout cut by a balanced k-d split (alternately along the longer extent) into 15 compact blocks of at most 80 so that each record stays within 400 vertices, numbered west to east; this block is centred +102 m east and -208 m north of the array centre. Layout: the detector positions are read from the vector graphic of Fig. 1 of the LHAASO Science Book (Chin. Phys. C 46, 030001 (2022), arXiv:1905.02773 v4, PDF page 8; the figure carries a NORTH arrow pointing up and a 150 m scale bar), which plots 5216 EDs as red squares and 1188 MDs as blue circles. The figure was registered by a similarity transform onto a second published copy of the layout, the right panel of Fig. 1 of arXiv:2401.01038 (X (m), Y (m) axes read from the tick labels): 5215 of 5216 EDs match within 2 m (median 0.16 m), scale 4.33 m per point, no rotation; the pool sides then measure 150.1 m, 150.1 m and 300.2 m x 110.1 m against the stated 150 m, 150 m and 300 m x 110 m. Origin: the centre of the circular array, the mean of circle fits to the outer ED ring, the 575 m ED boundary and the outer MD ring. With it, 4911 EDs lie inside 575 m and 305 outside (stated: \"4911 EDs ... radius of 575 m\" and \"305 EDs\" in the guarding ring) and the farthest ED is 635.2 m from it (stated outer radius 635 m). Placement: the origin is put at the coordinate the Collaboration gives for LHAASO, 29 deg 21' 27.56\" N, 100 deg 08' 19.66\" E (Science Book abstract, same document), in an azimuthal-equidistant projection (WGS 84) with x east and y north. An independent check: the three pools traced in OpenStreetMap (ways 1046559931, 1046559932, 1046559933, Overpass extract 2026-10-25T11:28:50Z) lie 1 to 3 m east and 2 to 10 m north of the pool corners placed this way. It is not stated whether the figure shows design or as-built positions and what point the quoted coordinate marks; accuracy_m 30 covers the OpenStreetMap offset and that doubt; the older coordinate 29 21 31 N, 100 08 15 E of the 2016 papers lies 164 m away and is superseded. Each MD is drawn as a 6 m square, the area-equivalent of the \"surface area of 36 m2\" of each muon detector in the Science Book (its tank is 6.8 m in inner diameter and 1.2 m high, arXiv:2405.11826): a position marker with the detector's area, not its outline. ",
  "name": "LHAASO KM2A muon detectors (MDs), block 9 of 15",
  "notes": [
    "Check: 1188 MDs (stated 1188); median nearest-neighbour distance 27.3 m against the stated 30 m triangular spacing; the farthest MD centre is 586.9 m from the array centre (the paper says MDs lie \"within a radius of 575 m\" for the zone of 15 m ED spacing)."
  ],
